[Music]  zelda's 35th anniversary is right around  the corner  and while that doesn't guarantee we'll  get any new information about breath of  the wild sequel anytime  soon there is at least an increased  chance of this happening  if and when nintendo announces a 3d  zelda collection it would be the perfect  opportunity  to share some additional info on the  development of breath the while too  just like they did with the announcement  of twilight princess hd in 2015.  yes anuma did state that we have to wait  a bit longer back when age of calamity  was announced  but that was five months ago what  constitutes as  quote unquote a bit longer i'd say close  to half a year definitely meets that  criteria especially considering that the  initial reveal of the game  is now well over one and a half years  ago time  sure flies with the anniversary now  closing in i thought it would be fitting  to revisit breath while 2's trailer  one last time and talk about something  many have wondered and theorized about  namely where could the entrance to the  underground cave system be  as well as the room where ganondorf is  located well today we will explore  just that uh i mean i i will be  exploring just that what is up  everyone it's your boy hyrulegamer oh  god what have i gotten myself into this  time  oh come on monster man we've been  talking about a collab for a long time  now what better timing than before the  35th anniversary  right but i just did a collab with mass  nintendo bandit  i don't know if this is the right time  i'll give you a free hyrule gamer  t-shirt  damn it sir you strike a hard bargain  you got yourself a deal  take it away before we get into possible  locations we first have to establish  some things about the reveal trailer  itself  monster maze addressed this before in  his video about the chronology of the  trailer  and that is that this doorway we see  right here is likely  not the entrance to the entire cave  system but instead leaves straight into  the room where ganondorf resides  some giveaways are the dim lighting and  rock walls and floor  which hints that this is already deep  underground somewhere but not out in the  open  second are the decorations of what seems  to be a boar-like figure  eerily similar to ganondorf's alter-ego  ganon  there are even more little details that  hint to this being true  but you'll just have to watch monster  maze's video for that which is an  amazing video by the way  just absolutely stunning work wait are  you purposely writing this in the script  to make me praise your video  no well alright then  anyway on to the next point ever since  the trailer premiered at e3 the main  consensus has been that the room where  the corpse is located  is in all probability underneath hyrule  castle somewhere but we do have to keep  in mind that these are just speculations  and nothing more  there was a recent fake leak about  breath of the wild too a supposed  pamphlet published by nintendo  stating that ganondorf is deep within  the caverns underneath hyrule's capital  but this is not legitimate information  it has since been revealed that this  wasn't an official nintendo publication  and wasn't even referring to the sequel  but rather the original breath of the  wild  regardless the chances of this room  being under the castle  is still very likely given calamity  ganon's nature of rising from the depths  of the castle and the fact that we see  malice flowing outwards from the corpse  it is the scenario that holds the most  way where the malice accumulates over  time  slowly building up until there is enough  of it to rise up to the surface and  launch another attack on hyrule's  populace  we also see the malice violently hit the  ceiling only to see hiro castle rise up  a few shots later  however we have to remain open to the  idea that the two events are completely  unrelated  maybe the castle doesn't even rise until  the later stages of the game  who knows until we get more information  on the game anything goes really  despite this we will still base our  predictions on this room being inside or  at least close to the castle  since as stated before based on the  little info we have it is the most  credible option by a long shot  with that in mind if the room containing  the sealed gerudo king is located here  then link and zelda have to be traveling  towards it from somewhere else  and judging by the sheer amount of  equipment they brought with them this  doesn't seem to be a short trip either  some of the things they are carrying  include bundles of wood cooking  equipment  mattresses and what seems to be a steel  lantern which kind of makes me wonder  why they are carrying torches and all  kinds of extra bags filled with other  stuff  from the other angle we can see a box  strapped to the animal in front of the  saddle  and another green tubular shaped object  in front of that which could be a tent  of some kind  we can even see link grabbing something  from one of the bags in this shot  it's not clear what it is even with the  enhancements to the image  but judging from the fact that they are  close to a water source i'd say it's  probably a water satchel to collect some  of that good old  h2o all this combined leads me to  believe that this is a trip spanning  across  multiple days why else would you bring  equipment to spend the night like  mattresses and even entire wood bundles  to build a campfire in real life cavers  usually don't carry equipment like this  as it would just get in the way unless  they are expecting a long expedition on  the ground  if the entrance to this cave system was  close to hyrule castle and say  ganondorf is located right underneath  the astral observatory  as an example you likely wouldn't need  this much stuff not to mention an entire  packing animal they could just dig  straight down into the underground  chamber from the numerous quarries  already present at the castle  instead the evidence suggests that the  cave's actual entrance is somewhere far  away from the capital and lincoln zelda  made a long journey  to ganondorf from there perhaps even  unaware that their path was leading to  the castle's depths  which brings us to the first candidate  in the list the giant hole inside the  yugaclan hideout  this location is definitely far enough  from the castle that it would require a  multi-day caving expedition to get there  some even suggest that this hole was  perhaps created with the sole purpose of  finding ganondorf's whereabouts  as far as locations around hyrule go  this and the chasms surrounding the  grudo tower nearby are the only things  close to a pre-existing underground  entrance with no visible  bottom definitely suspicious to say the  least  but there are also some problems with  this idea it's clear from the trailer  itself that the duo is moving along a  linear path towards their destination  not just a linear path but also a  horizontal one  they don't seem to be caving or  spelunking as it is often referred to  neither link or zelda is wearing a  harness nor are they seen carrying any  ropes  you might say well maybe they do but  they are in one of the bags on the  animal  which raises the question how did the  animal get down there  this creature bears a strong resemblance  to a rhinoceros at least in terms of  size i'd say it's probably even bigger  than that judging from the size  comparison  the average weight of a white rhinoceros  is already around 2  300 kilograms or 2.3 tonnes factor in  all of the equipment it's carrying and  you'd need quite a lot of rope and  effort to get this thing down here  the bottom of the ego hole isn't visible  but we can actually make a rough  estimate of how deep it is  in the champions ballad dlc link needs  to drop an orb into it to reveal a  shrine  after the orb is dropped it takes about  eight seconds until we hear the ball  activating the pedestal  we do hear the ball rattling beforehand  but it's likely hitting the side walls a  couple of times before it lands  it usually takes a second or so for the  pedestal to activate so  let's say seven seconds this is very  crude of course as there are multiple  factors that go into a calculation like  this  like the initial velocity and the ball  hitting the side walls which would slow  down a bit but we're going to do this  lazily  boom seven seconds that is about 240  meters or 780 feet high  two-thirds of the empire state building  or 160 tangles  that is quite a long way down you would  probably need at least three or four  ropes to balance and carry the weight of  this beast  which means close to a kilometer or .6  miles of rope to get the job done  alternatively since this is a fantasy  game they could have used the chica  slate to teleport the animal down i  guess  but first off we don't even know if that  technology is still working at this  point and second  the sheikah slate can only teleport to  shrines towers or a location  set by the travel medallion we know the  shrine is not inside the hole  only the pedestal so the only plausible  way would be if linker zelda climbed  down beforehand  set up a warp point with the medallion  and then teleported the animal down  while this is all possible it seems like  a lot of effort and busy work for  something they don't even know is going  to lead anywhere  so let's look at some alternatives  places that don't require hoisting a  multi-ton animal down and are more easy  to reach  like the underground trial at the great  plateau for instance  yes the shrine of resurrection serves  not only as a medical facility  but the entire room itself is also an  elevator that sends you  quite deep underground a lot more  convenient for bringing a large animal  and heavy equipment with you i would say  the shrine isn't as far from hyrule  castle as the yiga hideout but would  still span  all the way across hyrule field which  could still take a few days to get there  and back again  this would also be a way to have monk  mask kosher play an additional role in  the story  as he is the only monk not to disappear  into thin air once you complete his  test maybe he reveals a hidden path  somewhere in the underground trial which  leads into this cave system  or the elevator can go even further down  then we have two other viable locations  farron or somewhere inside the hebrew  mountains  fahren speaks for itself blah blah blah  zonai  not only would it tie into the zonai  motif we see sprinkled throughout the  underground caves but it would also be  far enough away from the castle to  warrant a long journey on the ground  we've already seen a doorway leading to  a shrine inside the spring of courage  so who's to say there isn't another one  of these doorways located somewhere  inside the dense forest of farren we  even see a bridge down in the caves that  looks like a larger variant of the  sargon bridge found above ground  a hidden entrance like this may lead  down more gently  as opposed to a straight drop or the  need for an elevator instead it would  slowly descend step by step  like a mine shaft next we have the hebra  mountains  care to take this one hg sure why not  now you might be thinking why hebrew of  all places  well once again he's gonna say it secret  doors  oh for a second there i thought you were  gonna say something else secret  zonai doors there we go yes while the  zonai are quite the cliche at this point  we can't ignore the zona architecture  down in the caves  some might think that hebrew doesn't  really have much to do with the zonai  aside from the north loma labyrinth  right  well actually we find a total of two  secret doors leading into the mountains  one leading to a shrine and the other to  the cave containing the hebrew great  skeleton and an additional shrine  in both cases the door features zonai  decorations on it the same ones found on  some of the other structures perhaps  there are more of these doors heading  somewhere within this massive mountain  range  one of which leading down and towards  hyrule castle the only problem here  would be the harsh temperature  i'm not sure if the packing animal could  handle the extreme cold  though we do see the great horned  rhinoceros in this region who have  adapted to the frigid conditions of  hebra  but until we know about this new species  of animal we can't say for sure if they  would be up to the task  either way if the entrance is located  here somewhere it would probably be of a  similar kind as the one found in farron  a gentle descent down into the earth  rather than a deadly drop down into the  abyss  lastly we have some honorable mentions  we have the shika towers themselves who  some furious like hmk have suggested  made double as an elevator leading down  they rose from the deep underground  after all so maybe they can also send us  down  similar to the shrine of resurrection  then we have the forgotten temple which  is already half buried deep inside a  canyon  it too could potentially hold a secret  entrance perhaps behind the giant hylia  statue  speaking of statues the eighth heroine  is another candidate  some believe this statue to represent  ganondorf and if true  what would be a more fitting location  for a secret entrance towards his sealed  corpse  than hidden behind a statue in his honor  those are all great options as well  which reminds me aren't you doing a  video about secret locations hidden  around hyrule i sure am  so if you will head over to my channel  where monster maze and i continue this  journey across  breath of the wild hyrule and look at  five mysterious locations and ruins  across hyrule and go into some mini  theories about them  awesome be sure to go check it out oh  and if you have your own suggestions as  to where this mysterious cave entrance  could be feel free to share them down in  the comments  i'm always interested in new ideas now  we could of course be totally  overthinking this 